# WORKFLOW RULES [CRITICAL]

Canonical procedures live in skills. This file states obligations only.

## Rule 32 — Bug validation

- Agent/skill: `bug-validator` / `.cursor/skills/bug-validation/SKILL.md`
- READ-ONLY validation; no automatic test-case or UI-automation pipeline
- Resolve environment via `environment-resolver` + `project-config.json` first
- Evidence: Confluence + optional OpenAPI under `config/swagger/` + code under `codeRoot` + optional DB
- Chat-first; disk report only if user asks

## Rule 35 — Test cases

Order:

1. Ask environment (from project-config) if not named
2. Ask Backend vs Backend+Frontend
3. `cross-dependency-finder`
4. `test-case-generator` → `test_cases/Backend/` (and Frontend if chosen)
5. `test-case-quality-validator` (≥ 80/100)

Template: `config/templates/Test_Case_Template.md`

## Rule 42 / 43 — Jira / Confluence REST fallback

MCP first; after retries use `config/scripts/*-rest.ps1` and disclose source line.

## Rule 44 — Linked Confluence on ticket analysis

Read linked wiki pages in the same pass as the Jira ticket.
